{"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE21numberOfSpanningTreesSdyF","symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ElectricalNetworks.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpectralGraphTheory\/ElectricalNetworks.swift#L19"},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"numberOfSpanningTrees"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"numberOfSpanningTrees()","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"SpectralGraphTheory"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"The number of spanning trees τ(G), weighted: the sum over spanning trees of the product of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their weights, which is any cofactor of the Laplacian (Kirchhoff’s matrix-tree theorem).","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Loops never lie on a tree; parallel edges each count. 0 for the empty graph and for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"disconnected one, 1 for one vertex."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/numberOfSpanningTrees()"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/numberofspanningtrees()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"numberOfSpanningTrees","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": counts pass "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" quickly (K₂₅ has 25²³). The Laplacian with one vertex removed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is eliminated densely as Grassmann, Taksar and Heyman eliminate (each pivot a sum of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"conductances, never a difference), so the count keeps a relative accuracy of about n · 10⁻¹⁶","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whatever the weights; its pivots are multiplied with the binary exponent kept apart, so it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"overflows only past ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s range, to ","type":"text"},{"code":".infinity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". When every weight is an integer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(unweighted included) and the count is below 2¹⁰⁰, it is computed exactly instead (two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"determinants modulo 62-bit primes, combined by the Chinese remainder theorem) and rounded"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once, so a count below 2⁵³ is exact. O(n³) time (less on sparse graphs), n² "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"numberOfSpanningTrees(as: UInt128.self)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns the exact count."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph/numberOfSpanningTrees()":{"url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/numberofspanningtrees()","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/numberOfSpanningTrees()","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of spanning trees τ(G), weighted: the sum over spanning trees of the product of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their weights, which is any cofactor of the Laplacian (Kirchhoff’s matrix-tree theorem)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Loops never lie on a tree; parallel edges each count. 0 for the empty graph and for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"disconnected one, 1 for one vertex."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"numberOfSpanningTrees","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"role":"symbol","title":"numberOfSpanningTrees()"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph","abstract":[],"role":"symbol","title":"Graph"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory","abstract":[],"role":"collection","title":"SpectralGraphTheory"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols":{"url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"role":"collection","title":"GraphProtocols"}}}